<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MathConverter.Demo.Demos.FlattenedOvalPage"
             xmlns:shapes="clr-namespace:MathConverter.Demo.Shapes"
             Title="If CornerRadius = ActualHeight, we get a flattened oval"
             Padding="20">
    <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,*" RowSpacing="20">
        <Label>
            This example doesn't really work in Maui. All you would have to do is:
&lt;RoundRectangle CornerRadius="{Binding Height, Source={RelativeSource AncestorType=Border}}" />

RoundRectangle will automatically clamp its CornerRadius to the minimum value of its path's height and width.
So, in fact, we have to make our own (in many ways, broken) UnclampedRoundRectangle so that we can fix it with MathConverter.
        </Label>
        <Border StrokeThickness="1" Stroke="Black" Grid.Row="1">
            <Border.StrokeShape>
                <shapes:UnclampedRoundRectangle CornerRadius="{Binding Height, Source={RelativeSource AncestorType=Border}}" />
            </Border.StrokeShape>
        </Border>
    </Grid>
</ContentPage>
